    "content": "\"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.\nItems, one per line:\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:question\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Does increasing the capacity of a neural ingredient-substitution model measurably improve its ranking of sustainable replacements, measured as Hit@1 on Recipe1MSubs [src_gismo_sizes]?\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_gismo_sizes\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:hypothesis\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"More capacity in a substitution ranker improves substitution ranking because larger encoders capture finer ingredient context, as LLM results suggest [src_llm].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_llm\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_lever\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hit@1 rises with width, reaching at least 22 percent at width 512, above GISMo's 20.56, and still climbing.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_not\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hit@1 plateaus near GISMo's 20.56 at every width; extra capacity adds nothing, so wider models are not the lever.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:test_summary\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reproduce GISMo's Recipe1MSubs result, then train the ranker at four widths 64, 128, 256, 512 with five seeds each on four GPUs; if Hit@1 climbs past the 20.56 baseline with width, compute is the lever.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:closest_prior\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Rita 2024 fine-tuned GPT-3.5 and TinyLlama on Recipe1MSubs, lifting Hit@1 from 34.53 to 38.03; no capacity sweep within one protocol exists [src_llm].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_llm\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:left_open\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Whether ranking quality keeps rising with model capacity inside one fixed protocol on Recipe1MSubs is unmeasured; the only scaling evidence is cross-protocol.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:anchor\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reproduce GISMo's published test-set MRR of 31.51 and Hit@1 of 20.56 using the official code, within 2 MRR points [src_gismo_gismo].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"src_gismo_gismo\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":31.51}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:limits\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Shows ranking accuracy on home recipes, not industrial formulations, and never measures actual environmental footprint or sensory quality of the substitute.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:src_gismo_sizes\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"Recipe1MSubs split sizes used by the plan\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:src_llm\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"the closest prior and the direction that larger models help\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:src_gismo_gismo\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"the GISMo MRR and Hit@k anchor the plan reproduces\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_train\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"training substitution samples\\\",\\\"value\\\":49044,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"samples\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Recipe1MSubs benchmark split sizes\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_test\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test substitution samples\\\",\\\"value\\\":10747,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"samples\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Recipe1MSubs benchmark split sizes\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\"}\n\nReturn only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type